.title  Multiplying without MUL: what a multiply costs, and where a table pays
.what   Two programs. MUL.ASM is lesson 22's flight with a meter in it: M sets the trap flag for one frame, and INT 1 - called after every instruction - counts the multiplies and divides by their opcode. Some eighty thousand a frame, near three seconds of an 8086 at 4.77 MHz, because the 8086 has no multiplier: a MUL is microcode shifting and adding once a bit. NOMUL.ASM takes them out of its busiest places: a divide by 256 is the middle two bytes of the product, and the ground's 2500 nodes are turned from tables built once a frame, because the sine and the grid's distances are known in advance. Two thirds of the divides gone, a third of the multiplies. And the famous table of squares, said honestly: on the 8086 it does not pay
.tier   LESSON
.main   NOMUL.ASM
.needs  MUL.ASM
.build  FASM NOMUL.ASM NOMUL.COM
.build  FASM MUL.ASM MUL.COM
.run    NOMUL.COM
.uses   IMUL IDIV PUSHF POPF LDS IRET ADC SBB
.engine ENGINE\E_M3D.INC ENGINE\E_RAST.INC
